&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;The Role of Advanced Equipment in PCB Manufacturing 
    &lt;div id=&#34;the-role-of-advanced-equipment-in-pcb-manufacturing&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#the-role-of-advanced-equipment-in-pcb-manufacturing&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Printed Circuit Board (PCB) industry has experienced rapid advancements, driven by the need for smaller, more complex electronic devices. As products shrink in size and grow in functionality, the manufacturing processes behind PCBs must evolve to meet new challenges. This article explores the critical role of chemical pumps and process control in modern PCB production environments.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
